# goodreads-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy this file to `.env` next to the scripts and fill in what you use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is in .gitignore. Keep it there. A secret passed on a command line
# is readable by anything that can run `ps` and lands in your shell history,
# which is why none of these has a flag you are expected to type.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#
#     explicit CLI flag  >  exported environment variable  >  .env  >  default
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any secret:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# Every variable below is one this code actually reads, and every variable
# the code reads is below. smoke_test.py asserts the two sets are equal in
# both directions.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: for all three modes you probably need none of them.
#
# Measured 2026-09-27 from a datacentre VPS: every listing kind, book pages
# and reviews were read with this file absent. AWS WAF did challenge book
# and search pages from that address, and real Chromium passed the
# challenge by itself in about two seconds. No key, no proxy, no account.
#
# What the credentials buy is insurance and volume: a solver for the day the
# WAF shows its CAPTCHA instead of its challenge, and more addresses than
# one for a run that would otherwise get one address scored.


# --- 2Captcha -------------------------------------------------------------
# One key, four separately-billed products: captcha solving, the Scraping
# Browser API, proxies and fingerprints. https://2captcha.com
#
# Solving here means AWS WAF's CAPTCHA, which 2Captcha solves with the
# AmazonTask / AmazonTaskProxyless task types
# (https://2captcha.com/api-docs/amazon-aws-waf-captcha). This repo has not
# met that CAPTCHA on goodreads.com: every WAF page it met was the free
# CHALLENGE action, so a normal run buys nothing.
#
# This key is also what --fingerprint uses. That is a separate subscription
# from solving.
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- Scraping Browser API -------------------------------------------------
# A remote browser you do not run or patch, with a persistent profile and a
# chosen exit country. Used by --cdp-endpoint.
#
#   country-  picks the exit country. Goodreads serves one English site to
#             every country, so this changes the address, not the data.
#   pid-      a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection each,
#             capped per account. Reuse pids rather than minting one per
#             run, and expect a 500 (`profile_locked`, exit 5) while another
#             run still holds this one.
#
# Selenium cannot use this: chromedriver's `debuggerAddress` takes a bare
# host:port with nowhere to put a password. Playwright and pyppeteer can.
#
# The credentials in a profile expire in about a day, so never paste a
# working one anywhere that is committed.
GOODREADS_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-de-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- Proxy ----------------------------------------------------------------
# One URL here, or --proxy-file with one per line for a pool. A pool is what
# spreads a run's volume, and --concurrency without one just sends N times
# the request rate from a single address, which is what AWS WAF scores.
#
# The credentials never reach the browser's command line: they go through
# the driver's own fields, and logs mask them while keeping host and port.
# Selenium's --proxy-server cannot authenticate at all, so that engine
# strips the credentials and warns.
GOODREADS_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@eu.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- Default target -------------------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url. Any page the scraper reads:
#
#   https://www.goodreads.com/list/show/1.Best_Books_Ever          a list
#   https://www.goodreads.com/author/list/656983.J_R_R_Tolkien     an author
#   https://www.goodreads.com/search?q=dune                        a search
#   https://www.goodreads.com/shelf/show/fantasy                   a shelf
#   https://www.goodreads.com/series/66175-the-lord-of-the-rings   a series
#   https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/5907.The_Hobbit            a book
GOODREADS_URL=https://www.goodreads.com/list/show/1.Best_Books_Ever

# Deliberately NOT here: an output prefix. `--out` already carries a
# non-empty default, so the loader, which only fills UNSET values, would
# never see it. The variable would be silently inert.
